   "Whether you're joining the workshop day or simply checking in for the conference, stop by and get set up early.\n\nPlease note that the workshop day wristband must be worn throughout the day. Badges must also be worn and remain visible throughout all three days of the Conj. If you are not checking in for the workshop day, you will not be permitted to enter the venue on Wednesday.\n\nAt the registration desk, you can request to have a label with your Discord or Slack handle printed and affixed to your badge. If you do not wish to be photographed, please request the appropriate sticker and place it somewhere clearly visible, ideally on your T-shirt or shirt."}
  {:session/time #time/zdt "2026-09-30T13:30-04:00[America/New_York]",
   :session/image
   "https://cdn.sessionize.com/image/92cf-400o400o1-h5iwi1d9yNDVAazq1XvV4G.jpg",
   :session/title "AI Tools & Practices Showcase",
   :session/description
   "This fast-paced session of attendee demos will be a showcase of tools and practices that are making a real difference for Clojure developers today.\r\n\r\nHour 1 talks: \"Just-in-Time Context for Agents\" by Lukas Domagala, \"The Philosophy of AI\" by Lorelai Lyons, \"Secret Sauce for Claude and Clojure\" by Jonathon McKitrick, \"Keeping Things Apart\" by Apollo Nicolson\r\n\r\nHour 2 talks: \"Wagoe the framework \" by Thijs Creemers, \"Leverage AI to do the nasty stuff\" by Santiago Cabrera, \"The Literate One-shot\" by Kimo K, \"ORC: A Lab for Self-Evolving Agents\" by Daryl Roberts\r\n\r\nHour 3 talks: \"Neither Gets the Last Word\" by Marc Limotte, \"Prompt: Play Tetris\" by Ag Ibragimov, ending with a speaker Q&A\n\n## Eric Dallo\n\nSoftware Engineer at Nubank, Emacs fanatic, NixOS enthusiast, and maintainer of some open-source projects like clojure-lsp, emacs-lsp, clj-easy and others, focusing on the developer experience.\r\n",
   :session/external-id "1261261",
   :session/subtitle "Eric Dallo",
   :session/location :location.type/w205abcd,
   :session/type :session.type/workshop,
   :session/capacity 500,
   :session/duration "PT180M"}
