  {:session/time #time/zdt "2026-10-02T16:20-04:00[America/New_York]",
   :session/image
   "https://cdn.sessionize.com/image/e172-400o400o1-YsheEmBHCWiD2n1D9mZ5La.jpg",
   :session/title "How to Make Things, and Why",
   :session/description
   "This is a talk about how to find flow, power, and joy in making software. It is about how to share the love of making with others, and how to nurture and protect communities of makers.\n\n## Stuart Halloway\n\nHe is a Clojure committer, and the architect of the Datomic database. Stuart was a founder and President of Cognitect (formerly Relevance).\r\n\r\nStuart has spoken at a variety of industry events, including StrangeLoop, Clojure/conj, EuroClojure, ClojureWest, SpeakerConf, QCon, GOTO, OSCON, RailsConf, RubyConf, JavaOne, and NFJS.\r\n\r\nStuart has written a number of books and technical articles. Of these, he is most proud of Programming Clojure.",
   :session/external-id "1275989",
   :session/subtitle "Stuart Halloway",
   :session/location :location.type/w207abcd,
   :session/type :session.type/session,
   :session/capacity 500,
   :session/duration "PT40M"}
